WEBVTT

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:32.940
What's wrong?

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:38.200
Hang in there! I'll call an ambulance immediately!

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:24.410
She's in almost the same condition as that body we found the other day.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.120
See that rope over there?

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.120
Whatever she went through prior to her death, it's the exact same thing as the other one.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.380
And her expression...

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:35.630
As with the previous body, I can't explain her facial expression.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:40.090
Both victims had the exact same facial expression.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:44.100
There's a high chance that we're dealing with a serial killer here.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:48.390
Hey, the station just called.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.900
Apparently, they've decided to hold a press conference.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.900
About <i>this</i> ?

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.690
Actually, there's more.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:00.410
A girl named Hashimoto Rumi was reported missing.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:04.660
Furthermore, Setamachi Police

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:09.660
are appealing for any information that might help find Hashimoto Ruri-san, who is currently missing.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.580
The bad news just doesn't end...

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:13.670
Hashimoto-san's family is praying for her safe return.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:19.590
I hope she's found alive at the very least...

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:20.170
Anyone with any information is urged to visit their nearest police box or station.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:29.680
I can't believe that Goto-san was actually dismissed.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.350
He refuses to follow orders from his superiors,

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.650
he sticks his nose into cases that are unrelated to his own,

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.690
and even though he manages to successfully arrest the culprits,

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:40.650
he doesn't actually reveal many details of the investigation itself.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.200
Guess you can't really blame our superiors for hating him...

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.910
Oh, that reminds me, where did they transfer him to?

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:50.830
As of today, I've been transferred to

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:55.250
the Criminal Investigation Division's Unsolved Cases Special Investigation Unit.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.170
Officer Ishii Yutaro reporting for duty.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:06.970
Excuse me...

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.980
Yeah, this is the Criminal Whatever-You-Call-It Unit.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.690
What? Hijikata? Who's that?

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.820
Detective Goto, that's the Chief!

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.780
Shut up! Pipe down.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.990
So? What does the Chief want from me?

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.870
What? Go to the Chief's office?

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.120
Just tell me what you want from me on the phone.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:34.710
You just woke me up from my nap.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.000
Right now, I'm really annoyed.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.720
I... saw one!

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:43.880
You saw...

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:46.390
a ghost?

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:51.020
Miki says that you know about these things...

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.140
so, please!

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.460
Hey, how's it going?

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:18.630
The weather's been pretty bad recently, right?

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:22.840
Want some?

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:25.220
Don't keep your personal items in here without my consent.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:26.800
This is my room.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.340
No, it isn't.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:31.640
This room belongs to the Film Club, remember?

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:34.430
But you're not a member.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.140
Well, that's just too bad.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:39.770
I sent an official request to the Student Society the other day.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:42.940
I'm now an official member of the Film Club.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.320
Why did you do that?

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.330
This is beautiful!

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:56.330
Say, why do you have this?

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.330
It's my mother's.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.840
Really?

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:06.670
Now that you've mentioned her, what was your mother like, Yakumo-kun?

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.720
There's just one thing I'd like to know.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:14.100
When did you start calling me by my first name?

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:18.940
Well, it feels strange to call you Saito-san even though we're the same age.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:21.810
And if I call you Saito-kun, it'll feel like I'm a lot older than you.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:24.070
Do whatever you want.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.570
In that case, I'll call you Yakumo.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.860
Who said that you could drop the honorifics?

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:31.240
Which means that "Yakumo-kun" is fine, right?

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.040
Looks like you missed a call.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.630
It's probably Goto-san.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:43.170
Oh! You mean that detective?

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:46.670
As far as I'm concerned, there are only two types of people...

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:53.140
Those who look at my red eye with fear, and those who try to use its power.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:55.010
I see...

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:57.140
Goto-san falls into the latter category.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:07:00.060
There's no need for me to go through the trouble of calling him back.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.270
Rather...

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.770
What kind of trouble did you bring with you this time?

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:05.780
What?

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:08.400
I-I didn't really bring any trouble with me...

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.030
Sorry, I'm coming in.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:13.280
If you're apologizing, then please leave.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.530
Shut up.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:15.740
Yo.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:17.120
Good afternoon.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:19.960
You're still involved with this weirdo?

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:25.340
If you don't start cutting your ties with him soon, you'll definitely be single until you at least graduate.

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:26.460
What?

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:31.260
I'd just like to clarify that it's not my fault that she doesn't have a boyfriend.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:32.300
What?

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:35.180
Her main problem is her personality.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:40.230
Why do I feel that you're both talking badly of me...

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.560
Excuse me...

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:43.690
And who are you?

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:45.060
He's my subordinate, Ishii.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.230
Ishii-san, eh?

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:48.860
Then, let me be blunt.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.070
You should send in a request for a transfer to another division immediately.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:52.240
What?

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:56.580
If you insist on staying with Goto-san, you'll only become hairier and start growing fangs.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.830
Eventually, you'll turn into a savage bear.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.870
I don't want to hear that from a blasted cat-student.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:04.040
So?

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:07.630
What kind of trouble did you bring with you this time?

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:09.840
Oh? I'm impressed you know that I brought trouble.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:13.340
You've yet to visit me for any other reason.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:15.890
You want me to start visiting you without a reason now?

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.720
Thank you, but I'd rather you didn't.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:18.680
So?

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:23.730
Oh, right. Actually, I want you to go somewhere with me.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.310
Now?

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.940
I'm afraid I can't.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:28.860
I already have a prior engagement today.

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:35.360
If you're referring to the girl just now, she quietly left the room a moment ago.

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:44.120
Looking at your expression, I guess it's not good news.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:47.130
No, that's not true at all.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:50.590
We've decided to check the place out today.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.260
Can you draw me a map?

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.510
Of course!

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:01.140
Haruka-chan's matured since I last saw her.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:05.310
Oh, so her name is Haruka?

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.610
I-I'm sorry.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:14.150
Anyway, Goto-san, could you please go over today's problem once more?

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.660
You want me to go over it again?

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:21.410
You jump backwards and forwards while telling your story. That makes it difficult to follow.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.410
It all started five days ago.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:29.420
We received a call that two people had collapsed in the road.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:35.760
Hijikata Makoto, a journalist for the Hokuto Shimbun, was one of the victims.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:39.510
Apparently, she was investigating the kidnapping and killing of those girls in the news.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:42.560
She was merely found to be unconscious.

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:46.100
The other victim was Ando Takashi, 43 years old.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.980
He was already dead at the scene.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:52.020
Autopsy revealed that he died of heart failure from a drug overdose.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.570
We commonly call it "death from shock."

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:57.070
Ando was a former doctor.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:00.070
Three years ago, he was arrested for synthesizing illegal drugs

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:04.540
for personal use as well as distributing them to others.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:10.840
We're not certain if he accidentally died from testing his newly-synthesized drug or if he committed suicide.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:12.960
But the main problem lies with that reporter.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:19.300
Her family is claiming that a ghost has possessed her.

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:24.310
So nowadays the police are investigating poltergeist cases too, eh?

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:26.600
Under normal circumstances, we wouldn't.

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:34.610
But it so happens that she's also the Police Chief's precious daughter.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:36.650
I see.

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:38.360
So that's how it is.

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:43.700
Chief Hijikata begged me to save his daughter.

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:54.090
Why did Detective Goto just divulge everything to some strange university student?

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.340
E-Excuse me...

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:06.850
Haruka-chan, eh?

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:24.780
Ayaka... the same name as my sister...

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:44.510
A-Are you Ayaka-san?

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:48.810
Stop?

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:51.520
What do you want me to stop?

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:56.980
I don't understand...

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:02.280
I don't understand the meaning behind your words...

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:13.170
As expected of the Chief's house.

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:15.750
It's totally different from an officer's dorm.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:18.380
I think we've had enough grumbling from a middle-aged man

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.960
who has no hopes of moving up further in this world.

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:20.800
Shut up.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:25.890
He should really hospitalize her.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:29.930
I believe the Chief of Police has his public image to worry about.

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:34.440
Besides, there isn't a hospital around that will believe you when you tell them that

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:35.810
your daughter's been possessed by a ghost.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:37.230
That's certainly true.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:43.860
Goto-san, please stay here.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:45.280
S-Sure...

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.680
It's Ando Takashi's ghost?!

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:10.260
There's no doubt about it.

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:14.480
His soul is trying to take over her body.

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:16.480
Is that even possible?

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.730
As far as I'm aware, no.

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:24.490
The most likely scenario will be that the body rejects the incoming soul.

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:25.990
What will happen then?

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:29.990
She'll weaken and eventually die.

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.370
Although, I'm not entirely certain.

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:36.500
It's the first time I've come across such a scenario.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:41.920
He's possessed someone because he strongly wishes to remain alive.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:42.760
In other words...

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:48.010
If it was a suicide, he wouldn't have possessed her.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:50.720
Is there any indication that he could've been murdered?

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:55.270
It appears they investigated that angle too, but they didn't get any hits.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:59.270
Either way, I can only save her if I know more about Ando Takashi,

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:02.860
and that includes the state of his body.

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:07.030
In other words, we need to visit that disgusting geezer.

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:11.370
Could you possibly be Saito Yakumo-kun?

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.620
I possibly am.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:15.910
I thought so!

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:19.080
I've heard all about you from that useless detective over there.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:22.000
You can see ghosts, right?

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:25.130
You've got a big mouth, haven't you, Mister useless-detective?

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:29.090
I'm genuinely interested in death.

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:34.140
If souls exist, then death is nothing but the soul departing from the body.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:37.230
And if that's true, then what binds the two of them together?

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:40.150
When exactly are the two separated?

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:46.110
I figure that you, who can see ghosts with his red eye, would know the answer to that-

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:48.150
Sorry.

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:51.530
I didn't know where to park the car.

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:53.240
You idiot.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:56.200
I was in the middle of an important discussion when you-

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.540
I think that's about enough idle chatter.

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:00.670
Now, regarding what I asked you over the phone...

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:04.460
This is the report on Ando Takashi.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.670
What about his personal effects?

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:10.380
His family took them along with his corpse.

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:14.260
They refused to take all his personal effects though, so those should be in the storeroom.

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:15.600
Where in the storeroom?

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:16.680
Beats me.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.770
If you want them, go find them yourself.

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:22.900
My hands are full at the moment with this Kidnapping and Killing of High School Girls Case.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:24.190
Ishii.

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:25.070
Yes, sir.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:26.230
Go find them.

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:27.990
Yes, sir!

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:37.660
That bastard's sure taking a long time.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:40.330
Why don't you help him?

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:42.420
No way. You go.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:47.090
Goto-san, why don't you try and be kinder to him?

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:47.920
What?

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:52.130
You haven't noticed?

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:55.890
He has feelings for you.

00:15:55.890 --> 00:16:01.730
I sense a strong emotion that's different than simple respect for his supervisor.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:03.310
What do you mean?

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:07.820
I'm just telling you what I saw and sensed.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:09.860
A-And that means?

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:14.700
Y-You've got to be kidding me!

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.490
We're both men-

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:18.160
Sorry it took me so long.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:22.660
Is something wrong?

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:25.630
N-No, it's nothing.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:31.170
So, these are Ando's personal effects.

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:37.430
I wonder what these keys are for...

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:39.930
They might be his house keys.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:42.600
In that case, his family would've taken them.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.730
Y-You're too close! I-Idiot!

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.940
I found this in between the pages.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:50.400
I wonder who she is...

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.530
Her name's Ayaka.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.280
How do you know?

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:55.910
Her cellphone strap.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:59.700
Ishii, look into that key.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:03.370
We'll look into this key and the girl in the photograph.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:05.250
Understood!

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.500
He's a detective as well?

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:12.760
I am Detective Goto's subordinate. My name is Saito.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:16.260
Oh my, you're one young detective.

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:19.010
Hey, Yakumo, make sure you take notes.

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:23.140
I'm sorry. He's still a beginner.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:29.230
Could your mother possibly be Saito Azusa-san?

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:31.530
How do you know my mother's name?

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.030
Where am I?

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:44.040
Then, Kinoshita-sensei, you're...

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.960
Twenty years have passed already,

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.790
but I still remember like it was only yesterday.

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:54.840
It's an incredible coincidence that you helped to deliver Yakumo.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.510
And your eye?

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.930
And your mother? Is Azusa-san doing well?

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:09.940
Yakumo...

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:13.360
My mother is missing.

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:17.780
She's been missing for more than ten years...

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:22.200
Ever since that night when she tried to kill me...

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:32.670
Hey, what are you doing?!

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:47.770
She was a really kind mother up until that night.

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:51.650
And yet, that night, she tried her very best to kill me.

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:57.490
I'm still unable to understand her.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.490
Doctor, I'd like to ask you a question.

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:03.490
When my mother gave birth to me...

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:09.580
how did she react when she saw that my left eye was red?

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:13.040
That's...

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:16.050
Doctor, please tell me.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.050
She...

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:27.060
She was terrified...

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:31.560
when she saw that her newborn had a left eye that was red.

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:43.570
Thank you, Doctor.

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:45.580
It appears...

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:50.460
that she didn't want me.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:55.460
Yakumo...

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:59.460
Y-Yakumo-kun...

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:28.990
Don't!

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:30.750
Don't stop me!

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:32.910
That was your mother's, right?!

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:34.500
You can't throw that away!

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:35.960
You don't know anything about me!

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:42.340
Yes, I don't...

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:44.840
I know nothing about you.

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:46.890
Of course I know nothing about you.

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:50.350
And that's because you don't tell me anything.

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:55.100
You're always carrying everything that's painful and sad by yourself.

00:20:55.690 --> 00:21:00.980
I don't know her reasons, but she's still your mother!

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:03.610
That's why... Please...

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:07.160
Don't do something that you'll regret...

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:28.180
I'm sorry.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:31.180
Yakumo-kun...

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:35.230
Here, you hold on to this.

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:36.190
But...

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:57.330
Even though you learned about your past, and harbor hatred for your mother,

00:21:57.330 --> 00:22:00.840
you still manage to resist the darkness...

00:22:01.550 --> 00:22:05.340
Though this <i>is</i> also a path of life...

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:08.800
Too bad your plan didn't work.

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:11.600
I've just found something to look forward to.

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:17.600
He, too, will eventually be swallowed by the never-ending night, just like his mother.

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:20.730
Tell the doctor that I...

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:22.360
Kinoshita-sensei?

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:28.820
I've found the perfect vessel for his daughter's soul to possess.
